<title>UK: HKG leading airport for Manchester air cargo trade.</title>
<headline>HKG leading airport for Manchester air cargo trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong dominates the rankings of airports by combined import and export tonnage going through Manchester, 1996 statistics issued by the airport show.</p>
<p>Total cargo handled at Manchester last year at 83,791 tonnes was 1.5 percent down on 1995.</p>
<p>Imports into Manchester were 0.2 percent higher at 41,788 tonnes but this was outweighed by a dip of 3.2 percent in exports to 42,003 tonnes.</p>
<p>The U.S. was the largest overall country market accounting for 27,266 tonnes of trade followed by Hong Kong.</p>
<p>The main airports for imports and exports compared with total 1995 traffic are:</p>
<p> AIRPORT	  IMPORTS    EXPORTS  '96 TOTAL    '95 TOTAL</p>
<p> HONG KONG	10,644	9,689     20,334	  20,622</p>
<p> CHICAGO O'HARE  3,351	3,430	6,781	   6,294</p>
<p> AMSTERDAM	 1,853	3,714	5,567	  10,567</p>
<p> JFK-NEW YORK    2,686	2,473	5,159	   5,746</p>
<p> ORLANDO	   3,076	1,755	4,831	   4,851</p>
<p> DUBLIN	    2,229	2,273	4,502	   2,415</p>
<p> ATLANTA	   1,667	2,806	4,474	   4,824</p>
<p> SINGAPORE	 1,294	1,862	3,156	   2,604</p>
<p> DUBAI	     1,292	1,510	2,802	   3,795</p>
<p> SANFORD/FLA     1,589	  913	2,502	    N.A.</p>
<p> NEWARK-NYK	1,256	1,020	2,277	     204</p>
<p> TORONTO	   1,032	1,022	2,055	   1,380</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	 1,314	  587	1,901	   1,354</p>
<p> ZURICH		719	  625	1,343	   1,546</p>
<p> PARIS-CDG	   569	  763	1,332	     952</p>
<p> LONDON-HEATHROW 1,054	  231	1,285	   1,199</p>
<p> TOTAL ALL	41,788     42,003     83,791	  85,101</p>
<p>DESTINATIONS</p>
